{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And he burned upon it the incense of spices.</b> Moses our teacher, peace be upon him, was the first to offer the incense and to offer the sacrifices. He offered all seven days of ordination, for thus the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded him concerning all the services: ״וערכת את ערכו״ — and you shall arrange its arrangement — ״והעלית את נרותיה״ — and you shall kindle its lamps — ״והעלית את העולה ואת המנחה״ — and you shall offer the burnt offering and the meal offering." "<b>And behold,</b> the incense was included among the rest of the sacrifices. And in all the other services the first priest was Moses, until the eighth day of ordination, when Aaron was inaugurated into the high priesthood and took his own portion. And so we find that Scripture calls Moses a priest, as it is said (Psalms 99:6): ״משה ואהרן בכהניו״ — Moses and Aaron among His priests."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The prooftext phrases in the final sentence are cited fragmentarily; they allude to commands from Exodus 29 and Leviticus 8 given to Moses during the days of ordination."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:08:07.209836031Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}